      "body": "## What\n\nAdds an XPU dispatch branch in `RMSNormGated.forward_xpu` that routes decode-shape calls to the fused `rms_norm_gated_decode` kernel (vllm-xpu-kernels side companion PR) instead of the generic Triton `rmsnorm_fn` path.\n\nGate: fp16, `x.shape` in ((16,128), (24,128)) (heads x head_v_dim), contiguous, `z` present with matching shape/dtype/device, `weight (128,)`, `bias is None`, `group_size is None`, `norm_before_gate=True`, activation silu/swish. Everything else falls through to the existing path unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\nModel: Qwen3.5/3.6-A3B (Gated DeltaNet linear attention). XPU-only dispatch path; no changes to CUDA/native code paths.\n\n## Validation\n\nTested on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, per-tensor fp8 on-the-fly quantization, 2x Intel Arc Pro B70 (Xe2) TP2, eager, chunked prefill: outputs byte-identical with the fast path enabled vs. the existing path; no regressions observed across a range of concurrent request batch sizes.\n\nCompanion PR: vllm-xpu-kernels (kernel side).",
      "changedFiles": 1,
